# pyro_sourcefrompoints

- Label: Pyro Source from Points
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 1 to 2
- Parameters: 41 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/pyro_sourcefrompoints.html
- Summary (EN): Adds values to a Float VDB by treating each input point as a sphere that updates the voxels it overlaps. With no geometry connected, it creates a single source from its own parameters. Available since Houdini 21.0.
- Résumé (FR) : Pyro Source from Points ajoute des valeurs à un VDB en traitant chaque point comme une sphère qui met à jour les voxels qu'elle recouvre.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: Float VDB to modify", "points (optional): geometry whose points act as sphere sources"]

- Key parameters: ["Method: how point values combine with the existing VDB (Set, Add, Minimum, Maximum)", "Radius: sphere size, scaled per point by pscale", "Center: source location when no geometry is connected", "Scale by Timestep: makes Add mode add the same total amount per second, even with substepping", "Amount: point density, scaled by the density attribute", "Falloff: ramp controlling how the value fades from the point centre to its radius", "Noise (Enable, Scale, Element Size, Element Scale, Offset, Pulse): modulates the value with noise", "Distortion (Enable, Scale, Element Size, Element Scale, Offset, Pulse): warps the sphere shape with noise"]

- Caveats: ["Does not activate voxels, so sources outside already-active areas have no effect", "Every point is evaluated against every voxel, so high point counts can be slow", "Requires DOP-level permissions; not in Houdini Core, included in Houdini FX, Apprentice, Indie and Education"]

